meta {
  name: tag: gatus (tapis-health)
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/gatus/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "pod",
    "pod_definition": {
      "image": "twinproduction/gatus:v5.36.0",
      "description": "Gatus pre-seeded to monitor the Tapis stack: Systems/Apps/Jobs/Pods healthchecks, this pod's own peek.pods URL (302 = up+gated), plus exotic DNS and TCP checks. Status codes were probed for real. In-memory storage (ephemeral). Edit /config/config.yaml to add more.",
      "time_to_stop_default": -1,
      "environment_variables": {},
      "volume_mounts": {
        "/config/config.yaml": {
          "type": "ephemeral",
          "read_only": false,
          "config_permissions": "0644",
          "config_update_mode": "always",
          "config_content": "# Gatus - Tapis health board. ${VAR} expands from environment_variables; ${pods:secrets:KEY} from secret_map.\nstorage:\n  type: memory  # ephemeral - history in RAM, wiped on restart\n\nui:\n  title: Tapis Health | Gatus\n  header: Tapis Service Health\n\nendpoints:\n  # --- Tapis core services: public /healthcheck endpoints return 200 + {\"status\":\"success\"} ---\n  - name: systems\n    group: tapis\n    url: https://tacc.tapis.io/v3/systems/healthcheck\n    interval: 60s\n    conditions:\n      - \"[STATUS] == 200\"\n      - \"[BODY].status == success\"\n  - name: apps\n    group: tapis\n    url: https://tacc.tapis.io/v3/apps/healthcheck\n    interval: 60s\n    conditions:\n      - \"[STATUS] == 200\"\n      - \"[BODY].status == success\"\n  - name: jobs\n    group: tapis\n    url: https://tacc.tapis.io/v3/jobs/healthcheck\n    interval: 60s\n    conditions:\n      - \"[STATUS] == 200\"\n      - \"[BODY].status == success\"\n  - name: pods\n    group: tapis\n    url: https://tacc.tapis.io/v3/pods/healthcheck\n    interval: 60s\n    conditions:\n      # pods /healthcheck returns 400 on direct/tenant-less calls; <500 = the service answered\n      - \"[STATUS] < 500\"\n\n  # --- This very pod's public URL: tapis-auth gated, so an unauthenticated probe gets 302 ---\n  - name: peekaping-self\n    group: pods-ingress\n    url: https://peek.pods.tacc.tapis.io/\n    interval: 60s\n    client:\n      ignore-redirect: true  # don't follow the OAuth redirect - we want to SEE the 302\n    conditions:\n      - \"[STATUS] == 302\"  # 302 = ingress up + tapis-auth gating (proves routing, not the app behind it)\n\n  # --- Exotic monitor types (non-HTTP) ---\n  - name: tacc-dns\n    group: exotic\n    url: \"1.1.1.1\"  # DNS server to query\n    interval: 120s\n    dns:\n      query-name: tacc.tapis.io\n      query-type: A\n    conditions:\n      - \"[DNS_RCODE] == NOERROR\"\n  - name: tacc-tls\n    group: exotic\n    url: \"tcp://tacc.tapis.io:443\"\n    interval: 120s\n    conditions:\n      - \"[CONNECTED] == true\"\n"
        }
      },
      "networking": {
        "default": {
          "protocol": "http",
          "port": 8080,
          "tapis_auth": true,
          "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"],
          "tapis_auth_return_path": "/",
          "tapis_ui_uri_redirect": true,
          "tapis_ui_uri_description": "Gatus - Tapis service health dashboard"
        }
      },
      "healthchecks": {
        "readiness": {
          "http_get_path": "/health",
          "http_get_port": 8080,
          "initial_delay_seconds": 5,
          "period_seconds": 10
        },
        "liveness": {
          "http_get_path": "/health",
          "http_get_port": 8080,
          "initial_delay_seconds": 30,
          "period_seconds": 15
        },
        "networking_requires_ready": true
      },
      "resources": { "cpu_request": 100, "cpu_limit": 1000, "mem_request": 128, "mem_limit": 1024 }
    },
    "tag": "tapis-health",
    "commit_message": "Gatus pre-seeded with Tapis health monitors: systems/apps/jobs/pods healthchecks, peek.pods self (302), exotic DNS + TCP. Real probed status codes; in-memory storage."
  }
}

docs {
  ## Gatus - Tapis health board (pre-seeded)
  
  This is what Peekaping *couldn't* do: the monitors are **baked into the config** (gatus is
  config-file driven), so the instant the pod is up it's already watching Tapis - no UI clicking.
  
  ### What it monitors (status codes are real - I probed them)
  | endpoint | type | check |
  |----------|------|-------|
  | systems / apps / jobs | HTTP | `200` **and** body `status == success` (content-aware) |
  | pods | HTTP | `[STATUS] < 500` - `/v3/pods/healthcheck` returns **400** on tenant-less direct calls; <500 just means it answered |
  | peekaping-self | HTTP | `302` with `ignore-redirect` - a tapis-auth-gated URL redirects an unauthenticated probe to OAuth; **302 proves ingress + gating, not the app behind it** |
  | tacc-dns | **DNS** (exotic) | resolve `tacc.tapis.io A` via `1.1.1.1`, expect `NOERROR` |
  | tacc-tls | **TCP** (exotic) | connect to `tacc.tapis.io:443`, expect `CONNECTED == true` |
  
  ### The tapis-auth monitoring gotcha (same as Peekaping)
  Gatus has no Tapis JWT either, so a gated pod URL is only ever a **302** to it. The Tapis
  `*/healthcheck` paths are public (real 200s), which is why those give a true app-level signal. To
  health-check a gated app's *insides*, point gatus at its **in-cluster** DNS (bypasses Traefik) or
  expose a public unauthenticated health path.
  
  ### Instantiate
  `POST /pods` with `{ "template": "gatus:tapis-health", "pod_id": "tapishealth" }`
  -> board at `tapishealth.pods.<base>` already showing all six checks.
  
  ### Tweak it
  Edit `/config/config.yaml` (config_update_mode=always -> applies on restart). Add endpoints,
  change intervals, or wire alerts (`alerting:` + `endpoints[].alerts:`). For durable history use
  the `v5.36.0-postgres` stack tag instead of in-memory storage. Other exotic gatus types:
  `icmp://host` (ping), `starttls://host:port`, `tls://host:port` (cert expiry via
  `[CERTIFICATE_EXPIRATION]`).
}
